      "text": "## Theory Meets Practice: Key Papers → Production Systems"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#021",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:distributed-systems:00-overview, git-history:distributed-systems:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "distributed-systems/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "distributed-systems/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:distributed-systems:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "distributed-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "distributed-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Distributed Systems - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Paper | Year | Key Idea | Production Use |\n|-------|------|----------|----------------|\n| Lamport Clocks | 1978 | Happens-before ordering without synchronized clocks | Causally ordered logs everywhere |\n| Vector Clocks | 1988 | Per-process logical clocks, detect causality violations | DynamoDB, Riak conflict detection |\n| Paxos | 1989/1998 | Consensus in asynchronous system with crash failures | Chubby (Google), CosmosDB internally |\n| FLP Impossibility | 1985 | Consensus impossible with 1 crash in fully async system | Motivation for Raft's design choices |\n| CAP Theorem | 2000/2002 | C + A + P not simultaneously achievable | Every distributed DB design trade-off |\n| Dynamo | 2007 | Eventual consistency, vector clocks, sloppy quorum | DynamoDB, Cassandra, Riak |\n| Bigtable | 2006 | Sorted string tables, LSM-tree, column families | HBase, Cassandra, RocksDB, LevelDB |\n| Spanner | 2012 | External consistency via TrueTime (atomic clocks) | Cloud Spanner, CockroachDB |\n| Raft | 2014 | Understandable consensus (vs. Paxos complexity) | etcd (Kubernetes), CockroachDB, TiKV |\n| Kafka | 2011 | Distributed commit log, consumer group model | Kafka everywhere; Event Hubs compatible |"
    },
